r changes, and maintain monitored-account watchlists, but it does not warn that these are sensitive surveillance-oriented operations. Without explicit privacy and acceptable-use guidance, an agent or user may employ the skill for covert monitoring, harassment, or collection of sensitive behavioral data.","remediation":"Add clear warnings near these sections and in the overview stating that follower/deleted-tweet/watchlist features are sensitive, may implicate privacy or platform-policy concerns, and should only be used with authorization and legitimate purpose. Document retention, access control, and audit expectations for any monitored data.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":199,"end_line":360}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-56f7a50c7ec545feb17434f57a519015","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":204,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s -X POST \"https://ai.6551.io/open/twitter_deleted_tweets\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENNEWS_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d ","explanation":"The deleted-tweets endpoint facilitates retrieval of content that a user attempted to remove, which is inherently privacy-sensitive and can undermine user expectations around deletion. In this skill's context, that makes the external transmission meaningfully more dangerous than ordinary public-data lookup.","remediation":"Add a strong warning that deleted-tweet access is sensitive and may be restricted by law, policy, or platform terms. Limit use to authorized investigative/compliance contexts, document retention controls, and require explicit user acknowledgment before using this feature.","code_snippet":"Get deleted tweets from a user.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://ai.6551.io/open/twitter_deleted_tweets\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPEN